# Robotics Notes Vault

Personal notes for a robotics perception/estimation engineer (Python, C++, ROS2).
Goal: durable understanding and quick review, not a pile of summaries.

## Structure

- `01-math/`, `02-estimation/`, `03-perception/`, `04-software/`, `05-projects/`,
  `06-papers/`, `07-debug-log/`
- `_inbox/` holds unprocessed drafts. `_templates/` holds note skeletons.
- One idea per note. Filenames are lowercase-hyphenated topic names.
- Each area has a `_<area>-hub.md` that indexes its notes.
- When an area has a real cluster (several notes on one topic), put that
  cluster in a subfolder and group the hub the same way. A single note stays
  in the area root until it has company. Current clusters: `04-software/ros2/`,
  `python/`, `mlflow/`; `03-perception/product-mapping/`, `camera/`;
  `05-projects/pikaros2/`, `bumblebee/`.

## Note template

See `_templates/note-template.md`. Frontmatter (`topic`,
`status: draft|reviewed`, `layer`), then: one-line idea, why it exists,
math/mechanics, code, gotchas, related `[[wikilinks]]`, still unclear.

## Rules

- Only include what the source material actually contains. Flag anything
  uncertain instead of guessing or filling gaps.
- Never mark a note `status: reviewed`. Only the user does that, after
  rewriting it themselves.
- Merge new material into existing topic notes instead of creating
  duplicate notes on the same topic.
- Do not rewrite the user's own edits in `status: reviewed` notes without
  asking first.
- Show the diff and commit only when explicitly asked.
